# Generic CAD MCP

`solidworks-mcp` is a **generic** SolidWorks automation surface. It must not become a Marengo, humanoid, or any other product-specific toolkit.

## Do

- Name tools, schemas, handlers, docs, and examples around SolidWorks concepts (mates, features, mass override, reference geometry, URDF *helpers* that take caller-supplied names).
- Accept joint/link/frame names, materials, and mass values as **caller inputs**.
- Keep demo assets under `.demo/` product-neutral.

## Do not

- Hardcode product names, robot families, limb sides, or joint trees (`marengo_*`, `right_shoulder_*`, humanoid link maps) into MCP tools, worker commands, schemas, or generated catalogs.
- Add Marengo-only scripts, fixtures, or “arm naming pass” workflows to this repo. Those belong in the consumer CAD/project repo.
- Bake humanoid kinematics, actuator SKUs, or vendor part numbers into default URDF readiness beyond configurable required-ref names.

## Boundary

CAD content in a consumer assembly may use any naming the owner wants. The MCP layer only provides generic rename / material / mass / frame operations to apply those names.